  "note": "Annual election of one-third of the Ballyclare Urban Council, January 1927. Four nominations were received for three seats; after the withdrawal of Mr. Huston Service there was no poll (Belfast Telegraph, 14 January 1927, p. 10). John Hill was a new member representing labour. Mr. Service, the vice-chairman, had been indisposed. Returned unopposed."
